Here's the relevant code from the page, describing how the `new-window` event is emitted and how `createGuest` handles referrers and load options.

## The `new-window` emit

Inside the internal window-open handler, options are merged, the event is emitted on the sender, and then the guest is either set up or created:

```js
options = mergeBrowserWindowOptions(event.sender, options)
event.sender.emit('new-window', event, url, frameName, disposition, options, additionalFeatures, referrer)
const {newGuest} = event
if ((event.sender.isGuest() && !event.sender.allowPopups) || event.defaultPrevented) {
  if (newGuest != null) {
    if (options.webContents === newGuest.webContents) {
      event.defaultPrevented = false
    }
    event.returnValue = setupGuest(event.sender, frameName, newGuest, options)
  } else {
    event.returnValue = null
  }
} else {
  event.returnValue = createGuest(event.sender, url, referrer, frameName, options, postData)
}
```

## The `createGuest` function

This function reuses an existing guest for a matching frame name, otherwise builds a new `BrowserWindow` and conditionally calls `loadURL`:

```js
const createGuest = function (embedder, url, referrer, frameName, options, postData) {
  let guest = frameToGuest.get(frameName)
  if (frameName && (guest != null)) {
    guest.loadURL(url)
    return guest.webContents.id
  }

  if (options.webPreferences == null) {
    options.webPreferences = {}
  }

  guest = new BrowserWindow(options)
  if (!options.webContents || url !== 'about:blank') {
```

## Referrer and `httpReferrer` / `loadURL` handling

The load options set `httpReferrer` from the passed referrer, and adjust headers for POST data (including detecting a multipart boundary):

```js
    const loadOptions = {
      httpReferrer: referrer
    }
    if (postData != null) {
      loadOptions.postData = postData
      loadOptions.extraHeaders = 'content-type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded'
      if (postData.length > 0) {
        const postDataFront = postData[0].bytes.toString()
        const boundary = /^--.*[^-\r\n]/.exec(postDataFront)
        if (boundary != null) {
          loadOptions.extraHeaders = `content-type: multipart/form-data; boundary=${boundary[0].substr(2)}`
        }
      }
    }
    guest.loadURL(url, loadOptions)
  }

  return setupGuest(embedder, frameName, guest, options)
}
```

### Key notes
- The referrer originates as `const referrer = { url: '', policy: 'default' }` in the raw window-open handler, then flows through to `createGuest`.
- A comment in the code explains why `loadURL` is skipped for existing webContents pointing at `about:blank` — the concern is that a `"navigation to \"about:blank\""` would clear the popup, since the opener may want to "synchronously script the popup."

